  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "sign-in#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "Signing in by an emailed code",
      "excerpt": "Ana asks to sign in on her laptop, and gets an email with a link and a 6-digit c",
      "text": "or no action after 20 minutes (tunable time)",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T02:03:39.429Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "5 wrong codes end the reques",
      "offset": 417,
      "edited": "2026-11-05T02:03:47.181Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T02:38:51.576Z",
          "html": "<p>Done: a pending sign-in request now also ends after 20 minutes with nothing done. <code>SPELL_SIGN_IN_MINUTES</code> sets the time, the way the server's other settings are set; the mail and the \"ran out\" message name it. (J46)</p>",
          "commit": "c9cacedeb"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T02:17:53.490Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "statusphere#code-1",
      "kind": "code",
      "label": "Statusphere, and Lexicons",
      "excerpt": "Status.spell, written by spell app lexicon read · 9 lines // Read in from the Le",
      "text": "it's \"created at\" is a required date",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T02:12:21.723Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "- its \"created at\" is a date",
      "offset": 335,
      "edited": "2026-11-05T02:12:24.985Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T02:38:52.598Z",
          "html": "<p>Done: <code>spell app lexicon read</code> now writes <code>- its \"created at\" is a required date</code>. The language didn't have <code>required</code> yet, so it's new, in English and Spanish (<code>una fecha obligatoria</code>), and means the same as <code>must not be empty</code>. Status.spell is regenerated. (J47)</p>",
          "commit": "c9cacedeb"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T02:17:54.598Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "statusphere#code-1",
      "kind": "code",
      "label": "Statusphere, and Lexicons",
      "excerpt": "Status.spell, written by spell app lexicon read · 9 lines // Read in from the Le",
      "text": "it's \"status\" is required text, with maximum length 1",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T02:12:47.231Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "its \"status\" is text",
      "offset": 314,
      "edited": "2026-11-05T02:13:10.679Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T02:38:53.597Z",
          "html": "<p>Done: it now writes <code>- its \"status\" is required text, with maximum length 1</code>. The length counts letters, so an emoji is one; Spanish: <code>texto obligatorio, con una longitud máxima de 1</code>. The two rule lines below it are gone. (J47)</p>",
          "commit": "c9cacedeb"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T02:17:55.684Z"
      }
    },
    "c4": {
      "anchor": "6-limits#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "6. Limits",
      "excerpt": "No public address yet, and no real mail: codes are read from the catcher. One re",
      "text": "while someone is \"connected\" watch the folder?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T02:14:29.654Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "A file edited by hand on disk shows in direct reads only after the server next reads it.",
      "offset": 464,
      "edited": "2026-11-05T02:14:42.833Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T02:38:54.556Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes, done: while a page reads a space direct, its files are watched (for 2 minutes after the last read), so a file edited by hand shows in the next read on both sides. The first read after a quiet spell also catches up on edits made while nobody was connected. It uses the storage's own watcher, not a new one. T17 closed; the Limits line is gone. (J48)</p>",
          "commit": "c9cacedeb"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T02:17:56.779Z"
      }
    }
  },
  "on": {}
}
